precept CurrencyExchangeRates

# A stateless data-only precept governing a single exchange-rate observation
# between a base currency and a quote currency. Each record represents one
# rate quote — the rate, the currencies it converts between, the effective
# window in which the quote is valid, and the source that published it.
#
# Exchange rates are reference data — workflow precepts that need to convert
# currency (invoices, shipments, settlement) read the rate at quote time and
# carry it forward. This precept governs what a valid rate record looks like:
# the rate is strictly positive, the base and quote currencies are distinct,
# and the effective window is well-formed.
#
# Currency codes are ISO 4217 identifiers. The `currency` domain type accepts
# any registered ISO 4217 code — USD, EUR, GBP, JPY, CHF, CAD, AUD, etc.

field BaseCurrency as currency default 'USD' writable
field QuoteCurrency as currency default 'EUR' writable

# Rate carries dynamic from/to qualifiers — the runtime enforces that whatever
# rate value the host application assigns has its qualifier currencies match
# BaseCurrency and QuoteCurrency. Optional because a record may be created
# before the first quote is posted.
field Rate as exchangerate in '{BaseCurrency}' to '{QuoteCurrency}' optional positive maxplaces 8 writable

field EffectiveAt as instant optional writable
field ExpiresAt as instant optional writable

# Source identifies the publishing authority. Central banks publish official
# reference rates; market data providers (Reuters, Bloomberg) publish realtime
# tradable quotes; Internal is for rates derived inside the host application.
field Source as choice of string("ECB","FederalReserve","BankOfEngland","BankOfJapan","BankOfCanada","ReserveBankAustralia","SwissNationalBank","Reuters","Bloomberg","Internal") default "Internal" writable

# RateType distinguishes the convention this quote represents.
#   Spot    — settlement T+2 (the standard FX quote)
#   Forward — settlement at a future date
#   Mid     — midpoint between bid and ask
#   Bid     — what the market maker will pay for the base currency
#   Ask     — what the market maker will sell the base currency for
field RateType as choice of string("Spot","Forward","Mid","Bid","Ask") default "Spot" writable

field Notes as string optional writable

rule ExpiresAt > EffectiveAt when EffectiveAt is set and ExpiresAt is set because "Expiry {ExpiresAt} must come after the effective time {EffectiveAt} — an exchange-rate quote with a zero or negative validity window is malformed"
rule BaseCurrency != QuoteCurrency because "Base and quote currencies must differ — converting a currency to itself is not a meaningful exchange rate"
